WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:10.100 --> 00:00:11.600
What’s good homeboy?

00:00:11.600 --> 00:00:15.780
This week we divin down da rabbit hole with "Alice in Wonderland" by Lewis Carrol.

00:00:19.180 --> 00:00:24.800
Alice chillin wit her sista and is ready to pass da f**k out when girl peep a swagged-out rabbit

00:00:24.800 --> 00:00:27.380
yappin bout how late he gon’ be. Whaaat?

00:00:27.380 --> 00:00:34.080
Alice follow dis busta down a rabbit hole, falls fo a long ass time, and end up in a hall with a buncha locked doors.

00:00:34.080 --> 00:00:41.380
Alice find a baby size key dat fits a baby size door, open dat bitch up, and peeps a fine-ass garden on da otha side.

00:00:41.380 --> 00:00:44.400
Problem is, Alice too damn thick to
get through.

00:00:44.400 --> 00:00:48.520
She spots a little cup o’ drank, give it a sip, and turns into an itty biddy.

00:00:48.520 --> 00:00:51.780
Oh sh*t! Now she can’t use dat baby size key!

00:00:51.780 --> 00:00:57.500
So then she peep a piece of cake dat say “EAT ME." Girl get her grub on, and ends up hella big.

00:00:57.500 --> 00:01:02.740
Since she still cain’t fit through da door, she start cryin and straight up floods da whole damn room.

00:01:02.740 --> 00:01:07.540
Girl picks up a fan, gets small again, and now she flowin in dat river o’ tears.

00:01:07.540 --> 00:01:12.580
After swimmin to safety and chillin wit some animal homies, Alice sees dat white rabbit again.

00:01:12.580 --> 00:01:17.220
Fool roll up on Alice thinkin she his servant and tell her to get her ass back home.

00:01:17.220 --> 00:01:23.640
Eventually, Alice truck it to da forest where she peep a giant Caterpillar chillin on a shroom chiefin some dank.

00:01:23.640 --> 00:01:29.800
Brotha give her the 411 on how this shroom work — one side make her big, the other side makes her small.

00:01:29.800 --> 00:01:34.260
Later, Alice peep some cat chillin in a tree with a sh*t-eating grin all up on his mug.

00:01:34.260 --> 00:01:38.820
Fool’s name is Cheshire Cat, and he give her directions to the March Hare’s party.

00:01:38.820 --> 00:01:41.540
Aw, hell yeah, CRISTAL B*TCHES!

00:01:41.540 --> 00:01:48.280
Up at da March Hare’s spot, Alice joins a tea party wit some otha hustlas: Da Mad Hatter and a sleepy ass mouse.

00:01:48.280 --> 00:01:53.340
Da Hatter say they ain’t neva gon' stop sippin on da tea cuz fo them, it’s always 6pm.

00:01:53.340 --> 00:01:55.380
Time dun lost his damn mind.

00:01:55.380 --> 00:01:59.680
Alice throw up tha deuce and cruises over to dat sweet garden she peeped at tha beginning.

00:01:59.680 --> 00:02:02.980
She runs up on da baddest bitch in da hood — Da Queen of Hearts.

00:02:02.980 --> 00:02:06.060
Girl wanna cut off everybody’s head fo no damn reason!

00:02:06.060 --> 00:02:11.260
Da Queen even accuse da Knave of Hearts of stealin some of her grub and puts his ass on trial.

00:02:11.260 --> 00:02:16.140
Alice take part fo a little while and finally say, “Hold up! Dat’s some bullsh*t right there.”

00:02:16.140 --> 00:02:22.640
Da Queen tell her to shut her damn face, but Alice like, “Bitch hop off my nuts. You just a pack of cards.”

00:02:22.640 --> 00:02:26.700
Tired of her stupid lip, da Queen try to ice Alice by smackin her round.

00:02:26.700 --> 00:02:29.600
Then SNAP —&nbsp;Alice wake up in her sister’s lap.

00:02:29.600 --> 00:02:33.540
Damn. What the hell was dis girl smokin...

00:02:33.540 --> 00:02:35.000
...and where can I get some?

00:02:38.380 --> 00:02:42.820
Lewis Carol wasn’t like most writers. First of all, dat ain’t even his real name.

00:02:42.820 --> 00:02:45.420
His mama called him Charles Lutwidge Dodgson.

00:02:45.420 --> 00:02:49.200
And second, playa got mad game at logic
and mathematics.

00:02:49.200 --> 00:02:53.240
Matta fact, years of slingin dat logic influenced da comedy up in dis book,

00:02:53.240 --> 00:02:57.360
like when da Queen and her posse arguing about cutting of da Cheshire Cat’s head.

00:02:57.360 --> 00:03:00.640
Da real joke come from what it actually mean to behead somethin

00:03:00.640 --> 00:03:03.760
and whether or not you can do somethin you ain’t understand:

00:03:03.760 --> 00:03:09.100
"The executioner's argument was, that you couldn't cut off a head unless there was a body to cut it off from:

00:03:09.100 --> 00:03:13.540
that he had never had to do such a thing before, and he wasn't going to begin at his time of life.

00:03:13.540 --> 00:03:19.220
The King's argument was that anything that had a head could be beheaded, and that you weren't to talk nonsense."

00:03:19.220 --> 00:03:23.320
The Queen's argument was that, if something wasn't done about it in less than no time,

00:03:23.320 --> 00:03:26.140
she'd have everybody executed, all round."

00:03:26.140 --> 00:03:28.680
Homies got all sortsa readings fo dis book.

00:03:28.680 --> 00:03:34.780
Some say dat we peepin legit dreams dat representin all da crunk and creepy sh*t Carrol got goin on in his dome.

00:03:34.780 --> 00:03:39.860
Otha scholars think all dis wackness is just a way to philosophize in a real artistic way.

00:03:39.860 --> 00:03:44.660
Maybe dat hard logic been applied to a crazy world just tryna make a bigger point:

00:03:44.660 --> 00:03:50.000
dat every hustla tryna find order in their life, but da world around em ain’t nuthin but chaos.

00:03:50.000 --> 00:03:52.500
This whole wonderland is batsh*t crazy —

00:03:52.500 --> 00:03:57.780
we got objects giving order to people, and we got time stopping like some type of lazy piece of sh**.

00:03:57.780 --> 00:04:02.480
But da world ain’t da only thing that's changin — we changin too, 24/7.

00:04:02.480 --> 00:04:05.680
All throughout dis book, Alice always tryna define herself

00:04:05.680 --> 00:04:09.820
and flippin sh*t cuz she cain’t pin nuthin down — even who she is.

00:04:09.820 --> 00:04:13.320
'Dear, dear! How queer everything is to-day! And yesterday things went on just as usual.

00:04:13.320 --> 00:04:19.380
I wonder if I've changed in the night? Let me think: was I the same when I got up this morning?

00:04:19.380 --> 00:04:21.760
I almost think I can remember feeling a little different.

00:04:21.760 --> 00:04:27.420
But if I'm not the same, the next question is 'Who in the world am I?' Ah, that's the great puzzle!''

00:04:27.420 --> 00:04:33.260
Truth is, we all a little like Alice in Wonderland — we grow, we shrink, we learn.

00:04:33.260 --> 00:04:36.560
Erry day we forced to confront a world dat look like it’s upside down,

00:04:36.560 --> 00:04:41.760
and all the while, we changin so much dat we can lose track of who we are if we ain’t payin attention.

00:04:41.760 --> 00:04:43.900
Dat ain’t an easy pill to swallow, yo.

00:04:43.900 --> 00:04:49.240
So follow da white rabbit back to my store and cop yoself some Thug Notes Gear. Peace padna!

